                <pb facs="0559" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6831/209: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-15T18:00:00+02:00">November 15, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 15—2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>64. <hi rendition="#italic">Modus vivendi</hi> signed. As it seemed preferable
                    not to include exceptions in the body of the agreement, I have proposed and
                    request the Department’s permission to address a note to the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs incorporating the language suggested in the Department’s
                    instruction 492, October 12 except for the omission of “sardines in brine”,
                    which the Greeks are willing to drop.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
